$mob
vn  29216
nm  anguillian
sh  an anguillian
lo  <58>A me<94>na<58>ci<94>ng<58>, e<94>el<58>-l<94>ik<58>e h<94>um<58>ano<94>id <58>fa<94>ce<58>s yo<94>u c<58>ol<94>dl<58>y.<0>
de
An anguillian glides through the deep water, its six-foot eel-like body covered 
in mottled brown scales and ending in a flat, finned tail. Short legs and wide 
six-toed feet tuck beneath it, while two upper appendages end in hard bony 
pincers. Its blunt, eyeless, jawless face is dominated by a circular mouth 
ringed with teeth, flanked by spiny fins, giving it the look of something bred 
in lightless trenches rather than mortal seas.
~
lv  78
sx  male
al  -375
act regenerator stay_area scavenger
aff blind swim
bf  no_eyes has_tail
rnk rare
sp  spec_bloodsucker

$mob
vn  29217
nm  anguillian
sh  an anguillian
lo  <58>A f<94>em<58>al<94>e a<58>ng<94>ui<58>ll<94>ia<58>n s<94>wi<58>ms<94> he<58>re<94>, h<58>er<94> bo<58>dy<94> co<58>il<94>ed<58> ar<94>ou<58>nd<94> a c<58>lu<94>tc<58>h o<94>f l<58>ea<94>th<58>er<94>y e<58>gg<94>s.<0>
de
This female anguillian moves through the deep ocean water with slow, guarded 
menace, her brown-speckled eel-like-but-roughly-humanoid body has a small 
cluster of soft, translucent eggs attached to it. Short legs and wide six-toed 
feet tuck beneath her long tail, while two upper appendages end in hard bony 
pincers. Her pincers flex at the slightest disturbance, and her circular, 
tooth-ringed mouth at the centre of her eyeless head opens and closes silently 
as she is on guard for anything foolish enough to come near her brood.
~
