$mob
vn  29221
nm  stone urchin sea-urchin
sh  a stone urchin
lo  <238>A stone sea-urchin clings to the side of the tunnel walls.<0>
de
The stone urchin clings motionless to the tunnel floor, half-buried among silt 
and broken shell as though it were only a jagged black rock. Long, mineral-hard 
spines radiate from its rounded body, each one dark at the base and pale at the 
tip with a faint venomous sheen. When the current shifts too near, the spines 
flex almost imperceptibly, waiting to pierce careless flesh.
~
