lo  <218>A <225>gi<189>an<153>t <147>se<141>a <135>an<99>em<105>on<111>e <147>cl<153>in<189>gs<225> t<218>o <225>th<189>e <153>ca<147>na<141>l <135>fl<99>oo<105>r,<111> h<147>er<153> t<189>en<225>dr<218>il<225>s <189>wa<153>vi<147>ng<141> g<135>en<99>tl<105>y.<0>
de
She waits among the stones and silt of the drowned canal, a vast sea anemone 
with a fleshy column anchored deep into the floor and a halo of long, luminous 
tendrils swaying gently in the current. Her colours are strangely lovely, all 
ghost-pink, blue-white, and bruised violet, but every soft movement hides a 
paralysing hunger. When prey drifts near, her tendrils close with sudden grace, 
drawing the victim down into the pulsing mouth at her centre.
~
