It goes "zip" when it moves, and "pop" when it stops, and, "whirrr" when it 
stands still. You have no idea what it is.
~

# OBJECT SETS

$objset
vn  29200
nm  Deepsea Healing
de
The Deepsea Healing collection was comissioned by good Eakos canal denizens who 
rescued and tended wounded travellers, to assist in their efforts. Its floating 
stone was said to draw restorative magic from the crushing depths, while the 
greaves and shield guarded healing sleepers from prowling things in the dark 
water. After the collective's dwelling was attacked and ater abandoned, these
three relics were scattered through the canal's drowned passageways, waiting to 
aid those brave and fortunate enough to recover them successfully.
~
ob  29247
ob  29248
ob  29249
ob  0
ob  0
bt  2
bt  2
bt  3
bt  0
bt  0
ap  sanc -1
ap  protect -1
# Rooms

$room
vn  29200
nm  Ota'ar Dar / Eakos Canal, Lower
de
<248>You are at the bottom of the ocean floor, in a deep canal between Ota'ar Dar's
<250>Arena / Prison canton and Eakos City.  Eakos City's walls prevent travel west,
<252>but you may travel north or east through the canal system, or upwards, towards
<254>the huge, looming area of darkness in the water above. To the immediate south
a huge iron grate has been installed to block access to the open ocean.<0>
~
st  underwater_ground
rf  none

