<144>A low, rounded tunnel in the bedrock opens at the base of an upwards shaft. 
<145>Here, canal stone gives way to smoother rock veined with pale shell and 
<146>pearl-coloured minerals. The water that fills this underwater passage is cold
<147>and clear, moving in slow pulses along a horizontal passage to the south. Faint 
<153>drifts of luminous silt stir cloudily up from the floor, revealing deep scrape
marks along the walls.<0>
~
